#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Monitor panel for the xfce4 panel button: every DDC/CI monitor on the desk with brightness up
front and contrast, colour preset, input, speaker volume, RGB gains and power behind a
disclosure, plus named profiles (Day / Evening / Night …) that set all monitors in one click.

Talks to the monitors with ddcutil (needs ddcutil and the i2c group; it says what is missing
otherwise). Monitors are matched to xrandr outputs through their EDID, so each row shows where
the screen sits on the desk. The bus↔monitor mapping and the monitors' capabilities are cached
in ~/.cache/monitor-panel so the panel opens instantly; profiles, monitor names and which rows
are expanded live in ~/.config/monitor-panel/config.json.
Clicking the panel button again, Escape, or clicking elsewhere closes it.
"""
